{%- comment -%}
  A date-first list of courses: one row per product, the date as the anchor of the row.

  WHY THIS SECTION EXISTS RATHER THAN mionas-collection WITH columns: 1:
  the native _product-card is a vertical media/title/price stack and a course row is a horizontal
  three-zone layout with no image at all; and mionas-collection's carousel, mobile_card_size and
  1-6 column settings are all meaningless on a course list, so a merchant would face a schema full
  of switches that do nothing.

  It borrows mionas-collection's frame: a free content_for 'blocks' region ABOVE the list, which is
  what carries the "PRÓXIMAS FECHAS" kicker as an ordinary mionas-text block rather than a baked-in
  heading setting. Same reasoning recorded in mionas-collection.liquid.

  COLLECTION SIZE IS STILL THE MERCHANT'S JOB: collection.products yields at most 50 products, and
  the past-date filter below runs in Liquid, AFTER that window. So the filter is a safety
  net, not a licence to stop drafting past courses -- if the collection ever grows past 50, the
  truncation happens in the collection's MANUAL order and future courses can be dropped before this
  section ever sees them.

  The header liquid and the rows capture below sort the collection's products by course_date,
  drop any whose date has already passed, and cap the result at max_products. When that leaves
  nothing to show, a merchant-editable fallback message renders in its place. Products with no
  course_date are excluded from the list and instead named in a theme-editor-only warning (see
  below), so a missing metafield surfaces as a visible prompt rather than a course quietly
  vanishing from the storefront.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign collection = section.settings.collection
  assign max_products = section.settings.max_products

  # WHY %Y%m%d AND NOT %Y-%m-%d: this one format has to serve two purposes. As a string it sorts
  # lexicographically into true date order (fixed-width, zero-padded, most-significant first), and
  # `| plus: 0` turns it into an integer for the past-date comparison below. Liquid has no reliable
  # string ordering operator, so the numeric form is the only safe way to ask "has this passed?".
  #
  # 'now' resolves in the SHOP's timezone, and Shopify's full-page cache means a course whose date
  # has just passed can linger for a little while past midnight. Accepted: the merchant also drafts
  # past courses by hand, so this filter is a safety net rather than the only mechanism.
  assign today = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0

  # Keys are "<YYYYMMDD>~<index into collection.products>". Sorting the keys therefore sorts the
  # products by date, and the index rides along so the product can be recovered afterwards. The
  # index tie-breaks lexicographically, so same-date rows can order as "~1, ~12, ~3" -- deliberately
  # unspecified, since the date prefix decides everything that affects the page and the index is
  # only a recovery handle.
  assign date_keys = ''
  assign skipped_products = ''

  for product in collection.products
    assign course_date = product.metafields.custom.course_date.value
    if course_date == blank
      # A product with no date cannot be placed in a date-sorted list. Skipping it silently is a
      # trap, so its title is collected for the theme-editor warning rendered below.
      assign skipped_products = skipped_products | append: product.title | append: '|'
      continue
    endif
    assign date_key = course_date | date: '%Y%m%d' | append: '~' | append: forloop.index0
    assign date_keys = date_keys | append: date_key | append: ','
  endfor

  assign sorted_keys = date_keys | split: ',' | sort

  if section.settings.background_color != blank
    render 'contrast-override', background_color: section.settings.background_color, section_id: section.id
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="section-background{% if section.settings.background_color != blank %} color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}"
></div>
<div
  class="
    mionas-course-list
    section
    section--{{ section.settings.section_width }}
    {% if section.settings.background_color != blank %}color-custom-{{ section.id }}{% endif %}
    spacing-style
    gap-style
  "
  style="
    {% render 'spacing-style', settings: section.settings %}
    {% render 'gap-style', value: section.settings.gap %}
  "
>
  {%- comment -%}
    Whitespace control on the tag is load-bearing: base.css hides
    .section-resource-list__content:empty, and a stray newline inside the div would be a text node
    that defeats :empty, leaving a --gap-sized hole above the rows when no block is added. Copied
    from mionas-collection.liquid, which carries the same note.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="section-resource-list__content">{%- content_for 'blocks' -%}</div>

  {%- capture rows -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      ORDER OF OPERATIONS IS LOAD-BEARING: sort, then drop past dates, then cap at max_products.
      A `limit:` on the loop above would take N products in the collection's MANUAL order and only
      then sort those -- with 12 courses and a max of 3, the page would show three arbitrary dates
      instead of the three soonest. The `rendered` counter is what applies the cap last.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign rendered = 0 -%}
    {%- for date_key in sorted_keys -%}
      {%- if rendered >= max_products -%}
        {%- break -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- assign key_parts = date_key | split: '~' -%}
      {%- assign key_date = key_parts[0] | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- if key_date < today -%}
        {%- continue -%}
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- assign product_index = key_parts[1] | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- assign course = collection.products[product_index] -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        One fixed id for every iteration -- see "WHY THE ROW IS A STATIC BLOCK" in
        blocks/_mionas-course-row.liquid. The product travels as closest.product, exactly as
        sections/mionas-collection.liquid passes it to its own static card.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% content_for 'block',
        type: '_mionas-course-row',
        id: 'static-course-row',
        closest.product: course
      %}

      {%- assign rendered = rendered | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  {%- liquid
    assign rows_content = rows | strip
  -%}

  {%- if rows_content == blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Collapsing to nothing would leave the page as a heading above an info panel with no
      explanation of where the courses went. The fallback line is a setting rather than hardcoded
      copy because it is the merchant's message, not the theme's.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.empty_message != blank -%}
      <p class="mionas-course-list__empty">{{ section.settings.empty_message }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="mionas-course-list__rows">{{ rows_content }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    THEME EDITOR ONLY. A product with no course_date is dropped by the loop above, and a course
    silently vanishing from the storefront is worse than an ugly warning in the editor. Guarded on
    request.design_mode so a visitor never sees it.

    The copy is English on an otherwise Spanish page, deliberately: it is merchant-facing tooling in
    the theme editor, where every other label in this theme's schemas is also English. It is never
    rendered to a shopper.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if request.design_mode and skipped_products != blank -%}
    {%- assign skipped_list = skipped_products | split: '|' -%}
    <p class="mionas-course-list__warning">
      {{ skipped_list.size }} {% if skipped_list.size == 1 %}product{% else %}products{% endif %} hidden — no “Course date” metafield set:
      {{ skipped_list | join: ', ' }}
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .mionas-course-list__rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .mionas-course-list__empty {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-role-body-lg-font-size);
    line-height: var(--text-role-body-lg-line-height);
  }

  /* Theme editor only -- deliberately loud, and never rendered on the storefront. */
  .mionas-course-list__warning {
    margin: var(--space-sm) 0 0;
    padding: var(--space-xs) var(--space-sm);
    border: var(--border-width-thin) solid var(--border-danger);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    color: var(--color-vermell-segell);
    font-size: var(--text-role-label-lg-font-size);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Mionas: Course list",
  "disabled_on": {
    "groups": ["header", "footer"]
  },
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@theme" },
    { "type": "@app" },
    { "type": "_divider" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "collection",
      "label": "t:settings.collection"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "max_products",
      "label": "t:settings.product_count",
      "min": 1,
      "max": 24,
      "step": 1,
      "default": 6
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "empty_message",
      "label": "Message when there are no upcoming courses",
      "default": "Próximamente nuevas fechas. Escríbenos para avisarte."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.section_layout"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "section_width",
      "label": "t:settings.width",
      "options": [
        { "value": "page-width", "label": "t:options.page" },
        { "value": "full-width", "label": "t:options.full" }
      ],
      "default": "page-width"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:settings.gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 28
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:settings.background_color",
      "placeholder": "t:settings.default"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:content.padding"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-start",
      "label": "t:settings.top",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding-block-end",
      "label": "t:settings.bottom",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Mionas: Course list",
      "category": "t:categories.product",
      "settings": {
        "section_width": "page-width",
        "max_products": 6,
        "empty_message": "Próximamente nuevas fechas. Escríbenos para avisarte.",
        "gap": 28,
        "padding-block-start": 48,
        "padding-block-end": 48
      },
      "blocks": {
        "static-course-row": {
          "type": "_mionas-course-row",
          "name": "Mionas: Course row",
          "static": true,
          "settings": {}
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
